course: dictionary
lesson: 4866
title: Ichthyosaurs, the sea reptiles that looked like dolphins
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ichthyosaur is a large sea reptile that lived long ago, at the time of the dinosaurs. You can work out a lot from the words around it: «Mary Anning dug out the first complete ichthyosaur at about 12.» It was something buried in the ground, and "complete" means every part of it was there.
explain: The phrase «ichthyosaur fossil» gives another clue. A fossil is the remains of a living thing that has turned to stone over a very long time. So an ichthyosaur fossil is the stony remains of one of these sea reptiles.
explain: The description also tells you what it looked like: a dolphin or a fish, with flippers, a long snout and big eyes. Those clues tell you its shape and how it moved through the sea.
explain: Be careful, because a clue can mislead you. An ichthyosaur looks like a dolphin, but it was a reptile, and it was not a dinosaur. The word "reptile" is the clue that tells you what kind of animal it really was.
fact: An ichthyosaur was a large sea reptile that lived at the time of the dinosaurs.
fact: It was not a dinosaur. It was a separate kind of reptile that breathed air.
fact: Ichthyosaurs gave birth to live young in the sea, rather than laying eggs.
fact: «Mary Anning» was a girl from Lyme Regis in England who found one of the first known ichthyosaur skeletons on the beach.
fact: A fossil is the remains of a living thing, turned to stone over a very long time.
exercise: «Mary Anning dug out the first complete ichthyosaur at about 12.» What was an ichthyosaur? | A kind of fish with no bones | A sea bird that could fly | *A large sea reptile that lived at the time of the dinosaurs | A dinosaur that lived on land
exercise: Ichthyosaurs looked a lot like which animal? | *A dolphin | A bear | A frog | A tortoise
exercise: «ichthyosaur fossil» is a phrase from the lessons. What is a fossil? | A new kind of sea shell | A toy made of stone | *The remains of a living thing, turned to stone over a very long time | A map of the seabed
test: Ichthyosaurs breathed air and gave birth to live young. Where did they live? | On dry land in the desert | Under the ice | High in the sky | *In the sea
test: «Mary Anning, a girl from Lyme Regis, England, found one of the first known skeletons on the beach.» What was Mary Anning? | *A fossil hunter | A zookeeper | A sea captain | A dinosaur hunter
exam: Why does the word "reptile" help you understand what an ichthyosaur was? | *It tells you what kind of animal it was: a reptile, not a dinosaur, even though it looked like a dolphin | It tells you the animal was a fish with no bones | It tells you the animal lived on land with the dinosaurs | It tells you the animal was a bird
